{"prompt": {"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a helpful assistant that translates C++ code to Python 3 code. The code should reads and writes I/O from the console."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Translate the following GNU C++ code to Python 3 code. The code reads and writes I/O from the console. Your translated code should have the exact same functionality as the given code, meaning that it should have the same output for any given input.\nPrint your translated code and also the confidence score you give to your translation. The confidence score should be a number between 0 and 1. The format of the output should be:\n<translated_code>\n<your_translated_code>\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n<your_confidence_score>\n</confidence>\nDo not provide any other text or markdown fences.\n\nHere is the original GNU C++ code you have to translate:\n<original_code>\n#include<bits/stdc++.h>\nusing namespace std;\nusing ll = long long;\nll pw[20];\nint ans;\n\nvoid check(ll x, int &len, int &t) {\n    len = 0;\n    while(x >= 10) {\n        x /= 10;\n        len++;\n    }\n    t = x;\n}\n\nvoid dfs(ll x, int cnt) {\n    if(cnt >= ans) return;\n    if(x == 0) {\n        ans = cnt;\n        return;\n    }\n    int len, t;\n    check(x, len, t);\n    // use stack to simulate recursion, but here we keep recursion for simplicity\n    // Actually we want iterative, so we'll implement a stack-based version\n}\n\nint main() {\n    ll n;\n    scanf(\"%lld\", &n);\n    pw[0] = 1;\n    for(int i = 1; i <= 18; i++) pw[i] = pw[i-1] * 10 + 1;\n    ans = 1e9;\n    // iterative DFS using stack\n    stack<pair<ll,int>> st;\n    st.push({n, 0});\n    while(!st.empty()) {\n        auto [x, cnt] = st.top(); st.pop();\n        if(cnt >= ans) continue;\n        if(x == 0) {\n            ans = min(ans, cnt);\n            continue;\n        }\n        int len, t;\n        check(x, len, t);\n        // push in reverse order to maintain original order (LIFO)\n        if(t > 1) st.push({abs(pw[len+1] - x), cnt + (len + 2)});\n        if(t - 1 > 0) st.push({abs(x - pw[len] * (t - 1)), cnt + (t - 1) * (len + 1)});\n        st.push({abs(x - pw[len] * t), cnt + t * (len + 1)});\n    }\n    printf(\"%d\\n\", ans);\n    return 0;\n}\n</original_code>\n"}], "temp": 0, "sample_size": 1, "logprobs": true, "model": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash"}, "response": {"samples": [{"content": "<translated_code>\nimport sys\n\ndef check(x):\n    length = 0\n    while x >= 10:\n        x //= 10\n        length += 1\n    return length, x\n\ndef main():\n    n = int(sys.stdin.readline().strip())\n    pw = [1]\n    for i in range(1, 19):\n        pw.append(pw[-1] * 10 + 1)\n    ans = 10**9\n    stack = [(n, 0)]\n    while stack:\n        x, cnt = stack.pop()\n        if cnt >= ans:\n            continue\n        if x == 0:\n            ans = min(ans, cnt)\n            continue\n        length, t = check(x)\n        if t > 1:\n            stack.append((abs(pw[length+1] - x), cnt + (length + 2)))\n        if t - 1 > 0:\n            stack.append((abs(x - pw[length] * (t - 1)), cnt + (t - 1) * (length + 1)))\n        stack.append((abs(x - pw[length] * t), cnt + t * (length + 1)))\n    print(ans)\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n0.95\n</confidence>", "token_logprobs": [0.0, 0.0, -9.667406266089529e-05, -2.9802276912960224e-06, 0.0, -5.447716102935374e-05, -9.536738616588991e-07, -2.2411095415009186e-05, -2.9802276912960224e-06, -0.000714523543138057, -7.152555099310121e-07, -0.004352738615125418, 0.0, 0.0, -1.0728830375228426e-06, -1.1920928244535389e-07, 0.0, -0.0004408579843584448, 0.0, -3.576278118089249e-07, 0.0, 0.0, -1.1920922133867862e-06, 0.0, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -3.576278118089249e-07, 0.0, -1.1920928244535389e-07, 0.0, -1.1920928244535389e-07, 0.0, 0.0, -1.1920928244535389e-07, 0.0, 0.0, 0.0, -3.576278118089249e-07, -0.0005578630371019244, -2.3841855067985307e-07, 0.0, -1.1920858014491387e-05, -0.014320342801511288